        "http://www.loc.gov/mads/rdf/v1#citationNote": [
            {
                "@language": "en",
                "@value": "p. 2 (a gravity map is made using numerous gravity measurements across the area of interest ... gravity measurements are often processed to a complete-Bouguer or isostatic gravity anomaly. These data are then gridded, so that the randomly spaced data are converted to a representation of the gravity field at equally spaced locations)"
